# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Market split problem {#market-split-problem}"
msgstr "マーケットスプリット問題 {#market-split-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The market split problem is a real-world, NP-hard resource allocation problem and has become a benchmark for quantum optimization algorithms.\n"
"It represents a high-stakes logistical challenge: how to partition a complex landscape of customers and products into manageable, equalized territories.\n"
msgstr ""
"マーケットスプリット問題は、現実世界のNP困難な資源配分問題であり、量子最適化アルゴリズムのベンチマークとなっています。\n"
"これは、顧客と製品の複雑な状況を、管理可能で均等化されたテリトリーに分割するという、リスクの高いロジスティクス上の課題を表しています。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The goal is to divide $n$ markets into two balanced sales regions such that each region receives exactly half the total demand for $m$ products.\n"
"The solution is the specific configuration that achieves the most even distribution of product demand possible, allowing a company to implement a logistics and staffing strategy where both regions are balanced,\n"
"minimizing the risks such as localized product shortages or warehouse overflows.\n"
msgstr ""
"目標は、$n$個の市場を、各地域が$m$個の製品に対する総需要のちょうど半分を受け取るように、2つのバランスの取れた販売地域に分割することです。\n"
"この解は、製品需要の分布を可能な限り均等にする具体的な構成であり、企業は両地域がバランスの取れたロジスティクスと人員配置の戦略を実施できるようになり、\n"
"局所的な製品不足や倉庫のオーバーフローといったリスクを最小化できます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the number of markets and products increases, the number of possible permutations grows exponentially, making it challenging to find the best split using traditional exhaustive searches.\n"
msgstr "市場と製品の数が増加するにつれて、可能な順列の数は指数関数的に増加するため、従来の網羅的探索を用いて最良の分割を見つけることが困難になります。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"
msgstr "数学的定式化 {#mathematical-formulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $A$ be an $m \\times n$ matrix representing the demand of products across markets, where $A_{ij}$ is the demand for product $i$ in market $j$.\n"
msgstr "$A$を、市場全体における製品の需要を表す$m \\times n$行列とし、$A_{ij}$を市場$j$における製品$i$の需要とします。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A binary assignment vector, $x = [x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n]^T \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$, is defined where:\n"
"* $x_j = 1$ assigns market $j$ to Region A.\n"
"* $x_j = 0$ assigns market $j$ to Region B.\n"
msgstr ""
"二値割り当てベクトル$x = [x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_n]^T \\in \\{0, 1\\}^n$を次のように定義します。\n"
"* $x_j = 1$は市場$j$を地域Aに割り当てます。\n"
"* $x_j = 0$は市場$j$を地域Bに割り当てます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let $d = [d_1, d_2, \\dots, d_m]^T$ be the total demand vector for each product, calculated as $d = A \\cdot \\mathbf{1}$. The target sales volume per region for product $i$ is exactly $\\frac{d_i}{2}$.\n"
msgstr "$d = [d_1, d_2, \\dots, d_m]^T$を、各製品の総需要ベクトルとし、$d = A \\cdot \\mathbf{1}$として計算されるとします。製品$i$に対する1地域あたりの目標販売量は、ちょうど$\\frac{d_i}{2}$です。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The optimization or feasibility constraint requires that the total sales allocated to Region A perfectly matches half the total demand for every product:\n"
msgstr "最適化または実行可能性の制約は、地域Aに割り当てられた総販売量が、すべての製品について総需要の半分と完全に一致することを要求します。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$A x = \\frac{1}{2} A \\mathbf{1} = b.$$\n"
msgstr "$$A x = \\frac{1}{2} A \\mathbf{1} = b.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In practice, because exact division is rarely possible, the problem is formulated to minimize the squared constraint violation (the cost function):\n"
msgstr "実際には、厳密な分割はほとんど不可能であるため、この問題は制約違反の二乗(コスト関数)を最小化するように定式化されます。\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\min_{x} \\left\\Vert{} A x - b \\right\\Vert{}^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n} A_{ij} x_j - b\\right)^2.$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\min_{x} \\left\\Vert{} A x - b \\right\\Vert{}^2 = \\sum_{i=1}^{m} \\left( \\sum_{j=1}^{n} A_{ij} x_j - b\\right)^2.$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expanding this gives a form that is equivalent to a quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) problem.\n"
msgstr "これを展開すると、二次制約なし二値最適化(QUBO)問題と等価な形式が得られます。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-26
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upon solving, the solution vector $x$ dictates to which region the market is assigned. This is the configuration that achieves the most balanced distribution of product demand possible.\n"
msgstr "解を求めると、解ベクトル$x$によって各市場がどちらの地域に割り当てられるかが決まります。これは、製品需要の分布を可能な限りバランスよくする構成です。\n"

